Aim:
To write a Java program to declare and initialize different types of variables and display their values.

Algorithm:
1. Start the program.
2. Declare variables of different data types such as int, float, char, and String.
3. Assign values to the variables.
4. Display the values using System.out.println().
5. Stop the program.

Program:
class Variables {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int age = 20;
        float marks = 85.5f;
        char grade = 'A';
        String name = "Sri";
        boolean result = true;

        System.out.println("Name: " + name);
        System.out.println("Age: " + age);
        System.out.println("Marks: " + marks);
        System.out.println("Grade: " + grade);
        System.out.println("Result: " + result);
    }
}


Output:
Name: Sri
Age: 20
Marks: 85.5
Grade: A
Result: true

Result:
Thus, the Java program to declare, initialize, and display different types of variables was executed successfully.
